    {
      "id": "hackernews-2026-09-22-robin-williams-daughter-to-fans-creating-ai-videos-have-some",
      "title": "Robin Williams' Daughter to Fans Creating AI Videos: 'Have Some Shame'",
      "summary": "Article URL: https://variety.com/2026/film/news/robin-williams-daughter-ai-videos-1236871568/\nComments URL: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49795718\nPoints: 42\n# Comments: 4",
      "body": "Zelda Williams is calling for fans to stop circulating AI-generated videos of her late father, Robin Williams, nearly a year after she last took to social media to ask them not to send her augmented content featuring the actor.\nIn a statement posted to X on Monday, the “Lisa Frankenstein” director wrote that a “supposedly ‘private video’” circulating of her father “is clearly AI, and not even particularly convincing AI,” she wrote. “Anyone who claims to be a fan who believes it clearly listened to his movies on mute because that voice is robotic and terrible. That said, a human made a robot create it, and to you I say: leave him out of your delusional bullshit and let him rest. If you cannot make your case without making a dead man make it more convincing for you, then tell me: who’s the one manipulating the public thru media now?”\nZelda continued: “I hate this cesspool of an app. It’s mostly bots and people willingly being duped by bots at this point so not sure why I feel the need to come back to clarify, but I love him, so I will. Just because he’s gone does not mean he’s now your puppet. Have some shame.”\nThe iconic comedian, who starred in films including “Jumanji,” “Good Will Hunting,” “Dead Poets Society,” “Hook,” “Mrs. Doubtfire,” and more, died in 2014 at the age of 63. In recent years, his likeness has become a popular target for AI recreation as users continue to create and share augmented videos of the actor.\nThis isn’t the first time Zelda has voiced her feelings about AI; Back in Oct. 2025, she wrote “Please, just stop sending me AI videos of Dad” on Instagram. “Stop believing I wanna see it or that I’ll understand, I don’t and I won’t. If you’re just trying to troll me, I’ve seen way worse, I’ll restrict and move on. But please, if you’ve got any decency, just stop doing this to him and to me, to everyone even, full stop. It’s dumb, it’s a waste of time and energy, and believe me, it’s NOT what he’d want.”\nJust last month, she revived her father’s Instagram account with siblings Zak and Cody in an attempt to “fight back against rampant AI abuse of his voice and likeness on here.”\nThat supposedly ‘private video’ of dad that I’ve been shown talking about conspiracies is clearly AI, and not even particularly convincing AI. Anyone who claims to be a fan who believes it clearly listened to his movies on mute because that voice is robotic and terrible. That…— Zelda Williams (@zeldawilliams) September 21, 2026",
      "source": "Hacker News",
      "category": "tech",
      "tags": [],
      "author": "CharlesW",
      "publishedAt": "2026-09-22T01:24:49.000Z",
      "imageUrl": "https://variety.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/robin-williams.jpg?w=1000&h=563&crop=1",
      "originalUrl": "https://variety.com/2026/film/news/robin-williams-daughter-ai-videos-1236871568/",
      "readTimeMinutes": 2,
      "language": "en"
    },
    {
      "id": "hackernews-2026-09-22-claude-status-elevated-errors-for-multiple-models",
      "title": "Claude Status – Elevated errors for multiple models",
      "summary": "Article URL: https://status.claude.com/incidents/7g1qpkyz5gxh\nComments URL: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49795579\nPoints: 117\n# Comments: 85",
      "body": "This issue has been resolved. Impact occurred from 5:50pm PT / 00:50 UTC to 7:10pm PT / 02:10 UTC.\nPosted Sep 22, 2026 - 02:35 UTC\nWe have seen success rates return to normal across affected models, and are monitoring closely to ensure no further issues.\nPosted Sep 22, 2026 - 02:11 UTC\nWe are continuing to work to resolve errors affecting some models. At this time, requests to Claude Fable 5 and 5.1 and Mythos 5 and 5.1 have returned to normal success rates. We are working to resolve remaining errors affecting Claude Opus 5, and will provide an additional update shortly.\nPosted Sep 22, 2026 - 01:35 UTC\nWe have identified the cause of elevated errors on requests to Claude Mythos 5.1, Claude Fable 5.1, and Claude Opus 5 and are working on a fix. We will provide an update as soon as possible.\nPosted Sep 22, 2026 - 01:17 UTC\nWe are investigating elevated errors on requests to Claude Mythos 5.1, Claude Fable 5.1, and Claude Opus 5. We will provide an update as soon as possible.\nPosted Sep 22, 2026 - 00:57 UTC\nThis incident affected: claude.ai, Claude API (api.anthropic.com), Claude Code, and Claude Cowork.",
      "source": "Hacker News",
      "category": "tech",
      "tags": [],
