      "id": "theverge-2026-09-21-california-tightens-rules-on-ai-data-center-energy-and-water",
      "title": "California tightens rules on AI data center energy and water use",
      "summary": "California Gov. Gavin Newsom has signed seven bills designed to prevent AI data centers from passing utility costs onto residents, as reported earlier by the Los Angeles Times. The package of laws requires the California Public Utilities Commission to introduce a new rate classification for data centers while forcing them to pay for upgrades to local power grids and water systems.\nOther bills incl",
      "body": "California Gov. Gavin Newsom has signed seven bills designed to prevent AI data centers from passing utility costs onto residents, as reported earlier by the Los Angeles Times. The package of laws requires the California Public Utilities Commission to introduce a new rate classification for data centers while forcing them to pay for upgrades to local power grids and water systems.\nOther bills included in the package will require proposed data centers to disclose their estimated water use to local governments, along with information about energy efficiency and drought planning. They must also meet certain energy, water, and fuel consumption requirements before qualifying for a streamlined approval process. Last week, Newsom signed an executive order to speed up the creation of an AI “kill switch.”\n“While the Trump administration moves toward deregulation, communities are left to deal with the consequences — higher electricity demand, grid constraints, water use, and pollution,” Newsom says in the press release. “With these laws, we are ensuring that Californians remain in the driver’s seat — and that those profiting from data centers aren’t doing so at our expense.”",
      "source": "The Verge",
      "category": "tech",
      "tags": [
        "AI",
        "News",
        "Policy",
        "Politics"
      ],
      "author": "Emma Roth",
      "publishedAt": "2026-09-21T20:29:45.000Z",
      "imageUrl": "https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/09/gettyimages-2286055476.jpg?quality=90&strip=all&crop=0,10.022372800543,100,79.955254398914",
      "originalUrl": "https://www.theverge.com/ai-artificial-intelligence/998453/california-ai-data-center-bills",
      "readTimeMinutes": 1,
      "language": "en"
    },
    {
      "id": "bbc-2026-09-21-watch-police-raid-organised-crime-targets-in-teesside",
      "title": "Watch: Police raid organised crime targets in Teesside",
      "summary": "Cleveland Police carried out one of their biggest raids in years, following the A66 crash that left two officers dead.",
      "body": "Cleveland Police have carried out one of their biggest raids on organised crime targets in years. About 130 officers were involved in the operation which saw 17 people arrested in the Middlesbrough area. The raids are part of a response to a crash on the nearby A66 last month, which resulted in the death of two officers in a police pursuit. Five men also died when their Volkswagen Passat went the wrong way down the road and hit a Cleveland Police armed response vehicle heading in the opposite direction.The BBC's Stuart Whincup was with the police as they carried out the arrests. Read more about the raids in this story.",
      "source": "BBC",
      "category": "world",
      "tags": [],
      "author": null,
      "publishedAt": "2026-09-21T20:21:29.000Z",
      "imageUrl": "https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/ace/branded_news/1200/cpsprodpb/50a2/live/d92ac8e0-b5f9-11f1-8e92-3520771561f6.jpg",
      "originalUrl": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/videos/c9x2z1m45vlno?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss",
      "readTimeMinutes": 1,
