      "id": "bbc-2026-09-21-other-generations-just-buried-it-youths-share-their-mental-h",
      "title": "'Other generations just buried it' - Youths share their mental health concerns",
      "summary": "The BBC's Catherine Burns spoke to some young mental health ambassadors who called for an increase in mental health support.",
      "body": "Accusations that those growing up today are a snowflake generation are wrong, the head of an independent review into mental health, ADHD and autism has said. Prof Peter Fonagy told the BBC that there had been a real rise in mental distress among children and young people, with anxiety, depression, self-harm and eating disorders the most common. His review was ordered nine months ago by Wes Streeting after the then-health secretary claimed in an interview that young people were over-diagnosed and \"written off\". The BBC's Catherine Burns spoke to some young mental health ambassadors who echoed the report's findings and called for an increase in mental health support.Read more here.",
      "source": "BBC",
      "category": "world",
      "tags": [],
      "author": null,
      "publishedAt": "2026-09-21T12:17:42.000Z",
      "imageUrl": "https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/ace/branded_news/1200/cpsprodpb/16e7/live/1b8f2f80-b5b6-11f1-b1d1-571ed4d7ff2c.jpg",
