      "id": "bbc-2026-09-21-inside-djibouti-refugee-camp-for-thousands-fleeing-houthi-ad",
      "title": "Inside Djibouti refugee camp for thousands fleeing Houthi advance in Yemen",
      "summary": "Fighting on Yemen's west coast has prompted thousands of people to flee by boat across the Bab al-Mandab Strait.",
      "body": "Fighting on Yemen's west coast has prompted thousands of people to flee by boat across the Bab al-Mandab Strait to Djibouti over the last ten days.The BBC's Frank Gardner visited a refugee camp in Obock, a small port town where officials are preparing for the arrival of up to 10,000 refugees.The UN International Organisation for Migration said people were ​travelling on overcrowded boats and arriving with very limited food and water. The crossings were sparked by an offensive by the Iran-backed Houthi movement to take control of a key island and seize the strategically important port of Mokha.Read more here.",
