      "id": "bbc-2026-09-20-townsend-run-over-by-pitch-roller-in-thailand",
      "title": "Townsend run over by pitch roller in Thailand",
      "summary": "Former England winger Andros Townsend jokes that playing Stoke away \"wasn't so bad after all\" following a bizarre incident before a game in Thailand.",
      "body": "Former England winger Andros Townsend joked that playing Stoke away \"wasn't so bad after all\" following a bizarre incident in Thailand in which he was run over by a pitch roller.The 35-year-old former Tottenham, Luton and Crystal Palace forward plays for PT Prachuap in Thai League 1.Townsend was warming up before a match at Pattani on Saturday when a member of staff appeared to lose control of a heavy pitch roller.Townsend's left leg briefly got stuck under the vehicle, but he was unhurt. He came off the bench late on in a 3-0 win., externalTownsend, who won 13 caps for England, made light of the incident on Instagram, referencing one of his recent posts in which he compared a sun-drenched Thai away trip with previous visits to Stoke's Bet365 Stadium.He wrote:, external \"It turns out Stoke away wasn't so bad after all. Swipe to see why.\"",
      "source": "BBC",
      "category": "world",
      "tags": [],
      "author": null,
      "publishedAt": "2026-09-20T09:08:43.000Z",
