      "id": "hackernews-2026-09-19-zk-jpeg-zero-knowledge-image-editing-and-compression",
      "title": "ZK-JPEG: Zero-Knowledge Image Editing and Compression",
      "summary": "Article URL: https://eprint.iacr.org/2026/2039\nComments URL: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49769405\nPoints: 96\n# Comments: 25",
      "body": "ZK-JPEG: Zero-knowledge Image Editing and Compression\nSteve Lu, Stealth Software Technologies, Inc.\nKimberlee Model, Stealth Software Technologies, Inc.\nJoseph Near, University of Vermont\nTools for generating deep fake photographs are proliferating with greater ease of use and prominence in pop culture. Image authentication tools can defeat these deceitful developments by verifying that a digital image was actually produced by a physical camera. The challenge is that these tools must be robust to desirable image transformations.\nCamera attestation uses digital signatures to prove an image's provenance from a camera. Lossy compression makes minute changes in order to reduce an image's size, and blurring or redacting regions of an image can protect its subjects. These changes invalidate an image's signature. Prior works use zero-knowledge (ZK) to prove a published image's edit history, but they do not survive lossy encoding such as the JPEG format.\nWe present \\zkjpeg, a cryptographic tool for JPEG compression that proves an image was correctly compressed from a secret, committed input. In addition, our tool can verify a large family of image transformations by integrating them into JPEG compression with minimal cost.\nOur system is fast, flexible, and can be instantiated from off-the-shelf ZK tools. We use PicoZK to convert Python image editing code into a ZK circuit for the line-point zero knowledge (LPZK) proof system.\nauthor = {Samuel Dittmer and Steve Lu and Kimberlee Model and Joseph Near},\ntitle = {{ZK}-{JPEG}: Zero-knowledge Image Editing and Compression},\nhowpublished = {Cryptology {ePrint} Archive, Paper 2026/2039},",
      "source": "Hacker News",
      "category": "tech",
      "tags": [],
      "author": "gslin",
      "publishedAt": "2026-09-19T19:23:23.000Z",
      "imageUrl": "https://eprint.iacr.org/img/iacrlogo.png",
      "originalUrl": "https://eprint.iacr.org/2026/2039",
      "readTimeMinutes": 1,
      "language": "en"
    },
    {
      "id": "bbc-2026-09-19-celtic-win-changes-game-but-can-they-reverse-rangers-derby-d",
      "title": "Celtic win 'changes game' - but can they reverse Rangers' derby dominance?",
      "summary": "Former Celtic captain Scott Brown believes a win for the Scottish champions against Rangers on Sunday \"changes the game\" after a turbulent week for Martin O'Neill's side.",
      "body": "With Yang Hyun-jun still on Asian Games duty with South Korea, Sebastian Tounekti and James Forrest have both been used on Celtic's left flank.But Brown believes the club's problems go beyond that. \"Rangers got in their face, they blocked Callum McGregor off and as soon as you block Callum McGregor off and you man-mark Cal, it's hard for anyone else to go and dictate.\"That's when you need a [Benjamin] Nygren to drop under, a [Mika] Baur to go and drop under and them do their job as well. You can't always keep looking at Cal to do everything.\"And Brown believes who starts best could be crucial.\"Rangers were up for the fight,\" he added on Sportsound. \"The first 15 minutes, it should be a battle. If you can go and win that battle, you can get the ball down.\"Celtic started very, very slow last week. They need to go back to basics, make sure they've got the fight, make sure they've got the hunger because they've got the talent - I know they've got the talent.\"You cannot have just one of those days against your biggest rivals, ever.\"",
      "source": "BBC",
